{:id :EACL-FORMAL-069
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "public-request/open-map-and-plural-delete-bare-record"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :fail-open
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before closed public request validation"]
 :affected-backends
 [:shared :datomic :datahike :datascript :third-party]
 :root-cause
 "Several public request maps were destructured without rejecting unknown fields, unsupported control values, or malformed object values. A misspelled consistency key therefore selected the default consistency, the reserved :page/basis :live control was accepted but ignored, the backend-only :allow-empty-schema? escape hatch crossed the public schema boundary, a misspelled relationship expiry was silently discarded and produced a permanent write, a bare Relationship record passed to delete-relationships! instead of the valid singleton collection [relationship] was mistaken for a page and became an empty successful write, tx-relationships accepted malformed envelopes as empty plans, a nil-ID object cleanup returned success without doing work, and delete-object! allowed a public envelope to carry the internal native-eid selector that the writer preferred over the public object."
 :fix
 "Validate closed request and endpoint shapes before dispatch, including the single-relationship convenience writer; require explicit sequential mutation batches; accept singleton collections while rejecting missing, nil, bare-record, and unknown-field envelopes; keep public-object and explicit native-EID deletion mutually exclusive; repeat mutation validation inside shared client protocol methods; and add a dedicated Dafny request-boundary model plus executed mutants and real-backend regressions."
 :closing-evidence
